# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Production build environment (Netlify)
#
# RELATIVE on purpose. The browser calls https://<netlify-site>/api/v1/...
# (same origin, HTTPS) and Netlify PROXIES it to the real backend defined in
# netlify.toml / public/_redirects:
#       http://32.236.114.49:3006/api/...
# This avoids "mixed content" (an HTTPS page cannot call an http:// API) and
# any CORS issues, since the browser only ever sees the same HTTPS origin.
#
# To switch backends: change the proxy target in netlify.toml AND
# public/_redirects (the http://...:3006 lines), then redeploy. Keep this
# value as "/api/v1" (do NOT set VITE_API_URL to the raw http:// backend on
# Netlify — that would re-introduce mixed-content blocking).
#
# Only if the backend is later served over HTTPS may you instead set
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend/api/v1 directly and drop the proxy.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_API_URL=/api/v1
